{
  "description": "Type each operation's 404/409 by what it means for that operation (DiskNotFound, SandboxNotFound, DiskAlreadyExists, SandboxStateConflict, ...) instead of the generic NotFound/Conflict, so callers catch the resource-specific tag. Statuses come from the published spec, plus 404 on addDiskUser/removeDiskUser, which the spec omits (the official SDK documents both against unknown disks). CreateApiToken's 401 is typed ApiTokenCreationForbidden: Archil only mints API keys from a console session, and answers an API key with a bare 401 even though the spec lists ApiKeyAuth. Each error keeps the body's `code`, and its `error` text as `message`: Archil answers `{ success: false, error, code }` (the spec's ErrorResponse). Live: forkSandbox on a sandbox with a mounted disk answered `409 {\"success\":false,\"error\":\"sandbox has mounted disks: disk dsk-… is mounted at /mnt/archil; stop the sandbox before forking it\",\"code\":\"sandbox_fork_mounted\"}`, and getDisk on an unknown id `404 {\"success\":false,\"error\":\"Disk not found\",\"code\":\"not_found\"}`.",
